+# Deploy: TipJar on Base + static site on IPFS
+
+Run everything from the repo root unless noted. Order matters: the site build embeds the Base contract address, so deploy the contract first.
+
+## 0. Prerequisites
+
+```bash
+nvm use                      # Node 22 (.nvmrc). Node 25 crashes the Next.js prerender.
+yarn install
+```
+
+You need:
+
+- A deployer keystore with a little ETH on Base: `yarn generate` (new) or `yarn account:import` (existing key). Check it with `yarn account`.
+- The address that should receive tips (ideally a multisig/cold wallet, **not** the deployer hot key). It is immutable in the contract.
+- `ALCHEMY_API_KEY` and `ETHERSCAN_API_KEY` (Etherscan v2 key, covers Basescan) in `packages/foundry/.env`.
+- For the site: your own Alchemy key and WalletConnect project id (both end up public in the JS bundle — restrict the Alchemy key in its dashboard), and a BuidlGuidl IPFS API key for the upload.
+
+## 1. Deploy the contract to Base
+
+```bash
+TIP_RECIPIENT=0xYourRecipientAddress yarn deploy --network base --keystore <your-keystore-name>
+```
+
+`TIP_RECIPIENT` is required on Base (the script reverts without it). This regenerates `packages/nextjs/contracts/deployedContracts.ts` with an `8453` entry.
+
+```bash
+export TIPJAR=$(jq -r '.transactions[] | select(.contractName=="TipJar") | .contractAddress' \
+  packages/foundry/broadcast/Deploy.s.sol/8453/run-latest.json)
+echo $TIPJAR
+
+# Check wiring onchain (expect Base USDC, your recipient, 0)
+cast call $TIPJAR "usdc()(address)"      --rpc-url https://mainnet.base.org
+cast call $TIPJAR "recipient()(address)" --rpc-url https://mainnet.base.org
+cast call $TIPJAR "tipCount()(uint256)"  --rpc-url https://mainnet.base.org
+
+# Verify source on Basescan
+(cd packages/foundry && forge script script/VerifyAll.s.sol --ffi --rpc-url base)
+```
+
+Commit `packages/nextjs/contracts/deployedContracts.ts` so every build uses the same address.
+
+## 2. Build the static site
+
+```bash
+export NEXT_PUBLIC_ALCHEMY_API_KEY=<your-alchemy-key>
+export NEXT_PUBLIC_WALLET_CONNECT_PROJECT_ID=<your-walletconnect-project-id>
+rm -rf packages/nextjs/out
+yarn ipfs:build
+```
+
+`yarn ipfs:build` = `NEXT_PUBLIC_IPFS_BUILD=true next build` in `packages/nextjs`, which:
+
+- targets Base only (`scaffold.config.ts`), so the burner wallet is off;
+- uses `output: "export"`, `trailingSlash: true`, unoptimized images (`next.config.ts`) → plain files in `packages/nextjs/out/`;
+- fails if `deployedContracts.ts` has no Base `TipJar`.
+
+### Check the build before uploading
+
+```bash
+cd packages/nextjs
+
+# Base contract address is in the bundle
+grep -rli "$TIPJAR" out/_next/static | head -1          # must print a file
+
+# Pages exist as directories with index.html (needed for IPFS gateways)
+ls out/index.html out/debug/index.html out/404.html
+
+# Smoke test the exact files locally
+python3 -m http.server -d out 3001
+# open http://localhost:3001 → header network shows "Base", no burner wallet,
+# stats/feed load from Base, connect a wallet → tip form shows your real USDC balance
+```
+
+## 3. Upload to IPFS
+
+```bash
+cd packages/nextjs
+yarn bgipfs upload config init -u https://upload.bgipfs.com -k <your-bgipfs-api-key>
+yarn bgipfs upload out
+```
+
+Copy the `CID:` from the output:
+
+```bash
+export CID=<cid-from-output>
+```
+
+(`yarn ipfs` does build + upload in one go; the split steps above let you check before uploading.)
+
+**Serve it from the root of an origin.** Next.js export uses absolute asset paths (`/_next/...`), so the site works on a subdomain gateway (`https://<cid>.ipfs.dweb.link/`), a DNSLink domain, or ENS + eth.limo — but **not** on path URLs like `https://ipfs.io/ipfs/<cid>/`. `https://dweb.link/ipfs/$CID/` redirects to the subdomain form, so it's safe to share. If the CID is v1 (`bafy...`) you can also use `https://$CID.ipfs.dweb.link/` directly.
+
+## 4. Post-deploy verification
+
+Run from `packages/nextjs` with `CID` and `TIPJAR` set.
+
+```bash
+GW="https://dweb.link/ipfs/$CID"
+
+# 1. Gateway resolves to a subdomain origin and serves the exact index.html we built
+curl -sSL -o /tmp/ipfs-index.html -w "%{http_code} %{url_effective}\n" "$GW/"   # 200 https://<cid>.ipfs.dweb.link/
+diff -q /tmp/ipfs-index.html out/index.html && echo "index.html matches"
+
+# 2. Every script referenced by index.html loads (absolute /_next paths resolve)
+for src in $(grep -o 'src="/_next/[^"]*"' out/index.html | cut -d'"' -f2); do
+  curl -sSL -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code} $src\n" "$GW$src"
+done                                                                          # all 200
+
+# 3. Other routes
+curl -sSL -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code} /debug/\n" "$GW/debug/"                 # 200
+
+# 4. Served bundle points at the Base TipJar
+f=$(grep -rli "$TIPJAR" out/_next/static | head -1)
+curl -sSL "$GW/${f#out/}" | grep -qi "$TIPJAR" && echo "contract address OK"
+```
+
+Then in a browser at `https://<cid>.ipfs.dweb.link/` (the URL printed by check 1):
+
+1. Header shows network **Base**; there is no burner wallet.
+2. "Tips go to" shows your `TIP_RECIPIENT`; stats and feed load.
+3. Connect a real wallet on Base, tip a small amount (e.g. `0.01` USDC): approve + tip succeed, the tip appears in the feed, and on Basescan the USDC transfer goes tipper → recipient:
+   ```bash
+   cast call $TIPJAR "tipCount()(uint256)" --rpc-url https://mainnet.base.org   # increased by 1
+   ```
